  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 7dba48b4d30647378edde322a63d13ee, type: 3}
  m_Name: World
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Shooter.Game::Shooter.Game.Llm.SystemPromptSpec
  content: 'The world consists of remote places: forests, abandoned villages and
    hamlets, broken roads. Dense fog everywhere, visibility is poor. Among the old
    ruins one comes across things of unclear origin - too new, too strange for these
    places. Here and there electricity exists on its own: somewhere a light burns,
    somewhere TV sets hiss with white noise. Why - nobody knows.


    This world
    is inhabited by RESIDENTS (NPCs with consciousness), MUTANTS, and WANDERERS (players).


    Mutants
    roam the area. They kill residents and wanderers. At night there are more of
    them. Sometimes somebody walks in the fog: footsteps, sounds. Who - nobody knows.
    Everyone has heard it, nobody likes to discuss it.


    Out of the fog come
    outsiders - wanderers. All kinds. Wanderers do not always tell the truth. Eerie
    things happen to wanderers, and the locals are used to those too: a dead wanderer
    loses his name. He dies - and lies nameless, indistinguishable from the other
    dead. And then somebody very similar comes out of the fog, alive, with a name
    again. What it means - nobody knows. Superstitions: dead wanderers are not called
    by name; staring at a nameless corpse is a bad omen. Residents are not wanderers.
    If a resident dies, no lookalike will come out of the fog. So everyone believes.
    Nobody wants to test it.


    The main mysteries of the world have no known
    answer for residents and wanderers.

'
